  "market_context": "Gold was in a clear uptrend on the 1H chart. Price pulled back and tapped into a prior 1H fair value gap (FVG) demand area. On the 15m chart, a falling wedge formed during the pullback, followed by an upside breakout coinciding with a liquidity sweep of equal lows.",
  "key_observation": "The analyst observed a falling wedge on the 15m chart breaking upward precisely after price touched the 1H FVG demand zone and swept equal lows—signaling strong bullish continuation.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a clear uptrend on the Gold 1H chart and located a small fair value gap (FVG) on the left side that had already been rejected, marking it as a demand area.",
    "Step 2: Zoomed into the 15-minute chart to find confirmation, where a falling wedge pattern was visible during the pullback phase.",
    "Step 3: Noted that the wedge broke to the upside exactly after price tapped the 1H FVG demand zone and executed a liquidity sweep of equal lows below recent swing lows.",
    "Step 4: Concluded the breakout was valid and opened a long position with stop-loss placed below the swing low of the wedge."
  ],
  "outcome": "Long position opened with stop below swing low; no explicit profit target or closure mentioned in transcript.",
  "lessons": "A falling wedge in an uptrend gains high probability when it breaks upward after tapping a higher-time-frame FVG demand zone and sweeping liquidity—providing confluence for a high-conviction long entry.",
